-- title:
--   Transported ℓ-levels agree only if e_γ stabilises K₀
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are distinct primes and $N$ a nonzero squarefree natural number divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ (`hrr`, `hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`).
--
--   **Base rings.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi$ an irreducible element, $\mathcal O$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next, $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ (written `Onr`) is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^r \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). Finally $\mathrm{vdet}:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (multiplicatively written) satisfies `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g$ is a unit of $\mathcal O$ times $\pi^n$, i.e. $\mathrm{vdet}$ is the $\pi$-valuation of the determinant.
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli.** $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite ($0<a$ or $0<b$) and is a division algebra exactly at the primes above $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), and $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it. The scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with its point-assignment $\mathrm{pt}$ is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure (`h𝒳`, whose clauses are the isomorphism-invariance, pullback-compatibility, surjectivity and injectivity on geometric points, and the universal property). An integer $n\ge 3$ is prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$, and $M\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{ptF}$ is a fine moduli space for such curves together with a full level-$n$ structure (`hM`); a group $G$ acts by automorphisms $\rho$ of $M$ with labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ realising the level-$n$ twisting action (`hρ`). The morphism $p:M\to\mathcal X$ is over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, is $\rho$-invariant, and forgets the level-$n$ structure on points (`hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$, $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ is a coarse moduli space for curves with an extra level structure at $\ell$ (`h𝒴`), and $d_0,d_1$ are the two degeneracy maps to $\mathcal X$, compatible with the structure morphisms and with the point-assignments, $d_1$ via $\ell$-isogenies (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`, `hd₀`, `hd₁`). The endomorphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ induce the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side.** $a_1,b_1\in\mathbb Q$ give a quaternion algebra which is definite and a division algebra exactly at the primes above $\bar r$ (`hdef`); $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1\le\Lambda_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$, $n_1$ an adelic unit in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), $\iota_0$ an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map into $M_2(K_0)$, and $v$ a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$. The group $\tilde\Gamma$ (`Γt`) is the group of units of $R_1$ away from $v$ (`hΓt`). Families $s_\ell$ of units and $s^{\mathrm f}_\ell$ of adelic units indexed by the primes $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ satisfy `hs`: the component of $s^{\mathrm f}_\ell$ at each prime not containing $r$ is $s_\ell\otimes 1$, its component at the primes containing $r$ is $1$, the product of the diagonal finite-idèle image of the scalar $\ell$ with $(s^{\mathrm f}_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}\,\Lambda_1\,(R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})\,\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; $\tilde\Gamma_\ell$ is the intersection of $\tilde\Gamma$ with its conjugate by $s_\ell$ (`hΓtℓ`). The unit $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\tilde\Gamma$ (`hwbar`). All rational integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and $\mathrm{coord}:\Lambda\to\mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)^2$ is an order coordinate system in the sense of `IsOrderCoord` (additive, unital, the twisted multiplication rule, injective, $r$-adically dense, and compatible with reduced traces).
--
--   **The special fibre datum.** $A_0$ is a fake elliptic curve with level-$N$ structure over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$, $X_0$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of height $4$ over that ring (`hX₀`), $\theta_0$ a system of formal coordinates of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and $\hat A_0$ is a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`). Maps $e,e':\tilde\Gamma\to\mathrm{End}(A_0)$ with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $\mathrm{deg}$ satisfy: each $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure (`hE1`); $e$ is multiplicative up to powers of $r$ (`hE1mul`); rational integral scalars in $\tilde\Gamma$ act by the corresponding $\Lambda$-multiplication up to powers of $r$ (`hE1sc`); conversely only scalars act by multiplications (`hE1'`); the induced endomorphisms of the formal module are, under any injective $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$, given by $g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$ up to powers of $r$, uniformly in $\gamma$ for one $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ (`hE2`); the action on a full level-$n$ structure is described by labels $\mathrm{lab}\,\gamma\in\Lambda$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$ (`hE3`); and every $r$-power isogeny pair of a fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$, preserving the level, comes from some $e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$ (`hE4`). A further order $R_2\le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators in $R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) is realised by endomorphisms $\hat e$ of $A_0$ over the base (`hê`), satisfying the group-law, $\Lambda$-equivariance and level clauses (`hE5a`), unitality, multiplicativity and the values on integers (`hE5b1`–`hE5b3`), the norm relation for conjugates (`hE5c`), the comparison with $e\gamma$ on $r$-power multiples of units (`hE5d`), and the joint matrix normalisation for $\tilde\Gamma$ and $R_2$ simultaneously (`hE5e`).
--
--   **Formal moduli.** $\iota:\mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a ring map, $\Phi$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map and of height $4$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`), $MD$ a moduli package for $r$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and $\eta$ assigns to each rigidified formal module a point of $MD$; `hη` has three clauses: on admissible rigidifications $\eta$ identifies points exactly for isomorphic rigidifications, $\eta$ is natural in the base ring, and every point of $MD$ is, locally on a finite cover of the base by principal opens, in the image of $\eta$ on an admissible rigidification. The injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ is height-normalised: there is an $m$ with $r^m\cdot M_2(\mathcal O)$ contained in the image and $r^m\cdot\mathrm{im}(E_0)$ contained in $M_2(\mathcal O)$ (`hE₀`). The family $\mathrm{eD}$ is a natural bijection (`hnatD`, `hbijD`) between the functor $\mathcal G$ of $MD$ on $\pi$-nilpotent noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras and the product of the functor corepresented by $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ with the formal upper half-plane functor $\Omega$ attached to $(K_0,\pi)$; its first component is the structural leg (`hfstD`), it converts the $\mathrm{GL}_2$-action on $MD$-points into the $\mathrm{vdet}$-twisted action on $\Omega$-points (`hGLD`), it converts a $\pi$-translate into a single Frobenius twist of the leg with unchanged Deligne datum (`hPiD`), and $\pi$-translates always exist (`hPiexD`). The map $\kappa$ compares $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ with $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatibly with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ is fixed. Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ over the special fibre is given by $A_{0w}$, $a_w,a_w',b_w,b_w'$ and $k_w$: $(a_w,a_w')$ realises the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), $(b_w,b_w')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw` gives one matrix $g$ normalising simultaneously the $\tilde\Gamma$-action and the composite $a_w\,b_w$, the latter matching $\iota_0(\bar w)$ up to powers of $r$.
--
--   **The comparison $\Xi$.** $\Xi$ assigns to each rigidified fake elliptic curve over a $\pi$-nilpotent noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with a leg $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ a $\mathcal G$-point of $MD$ over $B$, with: the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$ over connected $B$ (`hΞleg`); $\Xi$ is natural for pullbacks of rigidifications (`hΞnat`); $\Xi$ is invariant under isomorphisms of rigidified curves compatible up to $r$-power multiplications (`hΞiso`); and over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent $\Xi$ is computed by a rigidification transport of the formal module, with $j\le 1$, giving an admissible rigidified object whose $\eta$-image is $\Xi$ (`hΞdef`). A matrix $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is fixed, and the following compatibilities are assumed: translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ moves $\Xi$ by the action of $r^c\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ for some $c\in\mathbb Z$ (`heqΓ`); an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$, compatibly rigidified, moves $\Xi$ by $r^c\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$ (`heqW`); and the four clauses `hK1`–`hK4` assert, for the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted $\Omega$-coordinate of $\Xi$, existence of a rigidified curve over any given $\Omega$-point, uniqueness up to a compatible isomorphism, functoriality along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps, and lifting along a surjection with square-zero kernel. Moreover `hC0e` and `hC0u` give existence and uniqueness of the normalised level-$n$ transport of $P_0$ along a rigidification, $\Theta_{\mathrm f}$ assigns to a leg, an $\Omega$-point and an element of $G$ a nilpotent point of $fM$, natural in the base (`hnat`) and $G$-equivariant (`hG`), compatible with the fine moduli point of the transported level-$n$ structure (`hC2`) and, after composition with $p$, with the coarse moduli point of $E$ (`hC2c`); $\theta_t:\tilde\Gamma\to G$ is a group homomorphism, and `hC3` states that a $\gamma$-twist of an $\Omega$-point is realised by another rigidification of the same curve with the same leg, whose normalised level-$n$ transport differs from the original by the label $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$, and for which transported extra level structures at primes $\ell\ne r$ invertible on the base define the same subfunctor of points provided $e\gamma$ stabilises the base extra level.
--
--   **The data over $k$ and the assertion.** Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to k$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, $P,P'$ two $\Omega$-points over $k$, and $E,E'$ fake elliptic curves over $k$ with rigidifications $\varrho,\varrho'$ relative to the Frobenius twist of $\psi$ by $-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)$; the hypotheses `hΞψ`, `hev` and `hΞψ'`, `hev'` say that the legs of $\Xi\langle E,\varrho\rangle$ and $\Xi\langle E',\varrho'\rangle$ are that twist and that their $g_0^{-1}$-twisted $\Omega$-coordinates are $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ respectively. Further, $i:E\cong E'$ is an isomorphism over $k$ compatible with the group law, the $\Lambda$-action and the level-$N$ structure (`hi`, `hvia`); $\gamma$ is a unit of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ lying in $\tilde\Gamma$; $\varrho''$ is a third rigidification of the same $E$ with the same leg, whose $g_0^{-1}$-twisted coordinate is $(\psi,P')$ (`hev''`); $P'$ is the $\iota_0(\gamma)$-twist of $P$ (`htw`); $\varrho''$ is the $e\gamma$-translate of $\varrho$ in the sense of `IsTranslateBy` (`htr`); and `hcorr` provides a comparison of $\varrho''$ with $\varrho'$ along $i$, namely morphisms $ib$ on the reductions and $uA$ on the auxiliary curves, compatible with $g_b$, the structure morphisms and $g_A$, such that the two composites with $\varrho'.\varphi$ and $\varrho''.\varphi$ agree after multiplication by suitable powers of $r$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is: for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\ne r$ and $\ell$ invertible in $k$, every extra level structure $K_0$ at $\ell$ on $A_0$ and all extra level structures $C,C''$ at $\ell$ on $E$, if
--
--   (i) for every scheme $T$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(k/(\pi))$ and every $T$-point $R$ of the reduction $\varrho.E_b$, whenever $R$ composed with $\varrho.g_b$ factors through $C$ then $R$ composed with $\varrho.\varphi$ and then $\varrho.g_A$ factors through $K_0$;
--
--   (ii) the same condition holds with $\varrho''$ in place of $\varrho$ and $C''$ in place of $C$; and
--
--   (iii) $C$ and $C''$ define the same subfunctor of $E$: for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t:T\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $E$ over $t$, $R$ factors through $C$ if and only if it factors through $C''$;
--
--   then $K_0$ is stable under $e\gamma$: for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t:T\to\operatorname{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi))$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $A_0$ over $t$, if $R$ factors through $K_0$ then so does its image under $e\gamma$.
--
--   This is the detection half of the one-leg transport statement for extra level structures in the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of the fine family of fake elliptic curves: it converts the agreement of the two extra levels transported to $E$ along a rigidification and along its $e_\gamma$-translate into stability of the base-level $K_0$ at $A_0$ under $e_\gamma$. It is combined with its companion half in [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.forall_factorsThrough_iff_and_stable_of_isTranslateBy_corr_of_isAlgClosed_heightNormalised_eq_oneLeg`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.forall_factorsThrough_iff_and_stable_of_isTranslateBy_corr_of_isAlgClosed_heightNormalised_eq_oneLeg), which supplies the converse transport clause.
